  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7560214a2c335bd4e9cc29951d82c1e3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Victorina
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCInfoSO
  npcID: dona_victorina
  displayName: "Do\xF1a Victorina"
  characterFullName: "Victorina de los Reyes de Espada\xF1a"
  alias: La Doctora Victorina
  characterCategory: Filipino Elite / Socialite
  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 36afaede06121314da7a09f3ac2106c9, type: 3}
  description: A proud and highly pretentious Filipina socialite who imitates Spanish
    fashion and behavior. She is outspoken, easily offended and deeply concerned
    with appearances and social status.
  biography: "Do\xF1a Victorina attends Capit\xE1n Tiago\u2019s gathering with her
    husband, Don Tiburcio de Espada\xF1a. She wears an elaborate gown with a long
    train and carefully arranged curls, or frizzes. During the dinner, she becomes
    furious when Lieutenant Guevara steps on her dress and later criticizes his age
    and military rank. Her questions about Europe and her references to Spain reveal
    her desire to present herself as closely connected to Spanish society."
  characterFacts:
  - "She is married to Don Tiburcio de Espada\xF1a."
  - She is Filipina.
  - She imitates the clothing, speech and manners of Spanish women.
  - She wears an elaborate gown with a long train.
  - She is highly conscious of social position and appearances.
  - She becomes angry when Lieutenant Guevara steps on her dress.
  - She mocks Guevara for being old while still holding the rank of lieutenant.
  introductionLines:
  - "I am Do\xF1a Victorina de Espada\xF1a\u2014the Doctora, as people call me."
  - "This gentleman beside me is my husband, Doctor de Espada\xF1a."
  repeatDialogues:
  - lines:
    - They say the Chinese invented gunpowder centuries ago.
    - Surely such a well-known fact should not cause so much argument.
